## 4. Risk Assessment

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|------------|--------|-----------|
| Hook misbehavior crashes server | Medium | High | Document expectations clearly; use `PG_TRY()` guards in examples |
| Performance overhead from indirection | Low | Medium | Hooks are NULL by default → zero cost. Warn extensions about expensive logic |
| Multiple extensions overwriting hooks | Medium | Medium | Document that last one wins; future work: support chaining |
| Incorrect hook cleanup on unload | Low | Medium | Encourage resetting hooks in `_PG_fini()` |
| ABI compatibility across versions | Low | High | Use stable signatures; avoid passing internal-only structs |

> ✅ All integration points are marked as safe (impact 0.00), so structural risk is minimal.

